			PRINTFORMDW You glance at the boy, asking him if he recognizes the voice.
			PRINTFORMW 「...Mama?」
			PRINTFORMDW The boy's eyes close, clearly exhausted, and you share a relieved look with Shou.
			PRINTFORMDW within a minute a young-ish woman becomes visible around the corner of the path, clearly distraught and desperate.
			PRINTFORMDW Her eyes lock onto her son as soon as she sees the three of you, and with a wail of relief, she lunges forward.
			PRINTFORMDW She barely stumbles to a stop in front of Shou, eyes wild as she reaches for her son with trembling arms.
			PRINTFORMW 「Be careful. His arm was broken in a fall.」
			PRINTFORMDW Shou gently sets the child into his mother's arms.
			PRINTFORMDW She says nothing, eyes desperately scanning over every inch of her son's body as she clutches him protectively to her chest.
			PRINTFORMDW When her eyes reach the splint over his arm, she stops.
			PRINTFORMDW Robotically, her head turns up to look at Shou, comically dumbstruck. You'd laugh if the situation weren't so serious.
			PRINTFORMW 「Bishamonten-dono...」
			PRINTFORMDW Slowly, the woman starts to bend her knees.
			PRINTFORMW 「Please, do not kneel before me right now. You have a son to see too, do you not?」
			PRINTFORMDW Shakily, the woman nods, curling over her son.
			PRINTFORML 「Y-Yes, Bishamonten-dono, thank you Bishamonten-dono. I-」
			PRINTFORMDW Shou's kind smile is almost blinding.
			PRINTFORMW 「There are no thanks necessary. To see your son safely to you is all that I require.」
			PRINTFORMDW Carefully, you avoid rolling your eyes. Shou may be selfless by nature, but sometimes she really lays it on thick.
			PRINTFORMDW After a few more rounds of stuttered apologies, the woman turns back the way she came, her child clutched in her arms while Shou smiles after them.
			PRINTFORMDW Sighing, you clap her shoulder, and congratulate her for a job well done.
			PRINTFORMW 「What, I, well...」
			PRINTFORMDW Shou blushes, ducking her head.
			CALLF FIRSTTIME("ShouHelpKenji")
	ENDSELECT

ENDIF
